// SWARM RABBIT HOLE — Wave 13 (Impl-R): the seam-cell qualification
// rule (W2B §4.1: "seam cells = module-scope cells visible under the
// mode rules"). read_W/contrib operate on SEAM CELLS — module-scope
// Tier-L cells declared with an lcell_new initializer — because the
// R1/E0812 static analysis and the J(W) fold are defined over the
// module-scope seam, not over function-local state (wave-internal
// state must not escape the wave; NI(ii)). A function-local cell is
// wave-internal by construction: it is not a seam, and pretending
// otherwise is a checked refusal, not an unknown-name error.
// MUST FAIL TO COMPILE.

ptr seam = lcell_new(1)

fn main() {
    wave {
        ptr local = lcell_new(1)   // function-local: not a seam cell
        contrib(local, 1, 0)       // E-R1: not a seam cell
        int v = read_W(local)      // the same refusal
        contrib(seam, v, 0)
    }
    print("unreachable")
}
